{
  "primary_result_device_independence": "METHODS. IORN-007 (CPU, torch cpu) reproduces IORN-006 (GPU, torch cu128) 1.5 mm organ volumes on the same 40 series to a median ratio of 1.00 (pancreas 0.99), both TotalSegmentator 2.17.0. This is an independent validation that the ported segmentation is device-independent -- structurally the same claim as the G5 CPU/GPU bit-identity gate on the transport engine, applied here to the anatomy input.",
  "icrp89_not_a_requirement": "DISCUSSION, one paragraph. Agreement with ICRP 89 is NOT an IORN-007 requirement and is not a validation gate. IORN-007 computes dose on each patient's own segmented organ mass, so departure from a reference-phantom mass is the expected behaviour, not a defect: the spleen (+72%) and pancreas (-39%) figures are reproduced at fixed 1.5 mm with the same model, so they are not a resolution artefact, and per the handover a true model-vs-anatomy split would need a second segmentation *model*, not a second resolution (the same model at 3 mm shares the boundary-definition problem). The numbers are tabulated here as descriptive context only.",
  "reference": "ICRP Publication 89 (2002) adult-male reference organ masses",
